s chart in general  you can see that apple has always been  much more secure  so let me explain why apple has always  had  a huge focus on security and privacy  so let's start with that apple products  are very unique in the industry  because they continue to get software  updates for many many years  like for example you can still download  the latest ios 14 software update  for the iphone 6s which is now over  5 years old and on the mac you can  download big sur  on macs going all the way back to 2013  and making it even better they continue  to give you security updates on macs  that are even older than that for  example they just released new security  updates  for the old mac os catalina and mojave  software versions and on top of that mac  os  itself is just a whole lot more secure  most changes to the settings and  security options on your mac  require you to enter your password or  authenticate  to even get access to those settings  basically making it  extremely hard for any form of malware  to get into your mac and start changing  settings or deleting files  on windows you don't have that so many  people had issues with  viruses literally taking over control  of their computers apple also has  security in place for third-party apps  downloaded off of the internet  where you have to go into the settings  and manually unlock the privacy section  to even open the app which is something  that windows  doesn't do apple's latest macs also have  built-in  encryption which encrypts the drive and  keeps your data secure  so going back to the chart there's a  reason why there's such a huge  difference  between the amount of malware on mac os  versus  windows since apple has always been so  secure  it was never worth it to make malware  for the mac  because you could end up spending a  bunch of time writing the malware code  and never get anywhere instead if those  malware developers focused on windows  the return on investment would be much  much  higher so that's exactly what happened  it seems like the only reason we're  seeing  a big spike within the last year is  because malware developers can now  purchase  ready-made malware code and simply  adjust it to their needs instead of  starting from scratch  but the good news is that apple has  recently been making huge advancements  in security and privacy  and they're not stopping anytime soon a  couple of years back  apple updated safari with a new feature  called intelligent tracking prevention  which basically stops advertisers from  using cookies  to track you across the web and  apparently it's been doing an  absolutely excellent job at protecting  your privacy  like causing an ad firm to lose as much  as 25 million dollars  in advertising revenue and more recently  apple's added  a small little icon on your iphone that  shows when an app is accessing your  microphone or your camera  and many apps have already been caught  snooping in  on users privacy in the background and  now apple is forcing developers to add a  new  app data privacy label on every single  app on the app store  forcing them to disclose exactly what  they're tracking on your phone  which helps make iphones even more  secure going even deeper  apple recently added a new pop-up when  an advertiser or app  wants to track you across the web which  basically started a war between apple  and facebook  and long story short apple is winning  and facebook is starting to give in  so this shows just how serious apple has  been recently  in terms of security and privacy  but now i want to focus a bit more on  the mac  going back to that chart you'll notice  that the amount of new malware being  developed in 2021  has dropped significantly only around  2500 so far this year this basically  shows that the huge numbers last year  were probably an anomaly and i  personally think that the malware  developers  are leaving for one specific reason so  let's get right into that  as most of you know apple is going to  transition all of their macs over to  their own  apple silicon chips and if you didn't  already know what that is  apple is basically taking an iphone chip  suping it up and then putting it into a  mac  so the new m1 max literally have  very powerful custom iphone chips inside  of them  and as we know iphones are incredibly  secure being very very difficult  to hack into in fact they're so secure  that the fbi often has issues breaking  into iphones  when doing investigations and apple  refuses to help them  because of their dedication to the  privacy of their customers  going as far as to deny the fbi going  further  the app store is also really secure  since it has very strict guidelines for  app development  compared to the android store which will  basically accept  any app out there and in a recent  security comparison done by nordvpn  the iphone 1 and basically every  category  being much more secure and all of that  incredible security  from the iphone is now moving over to  the mac  with the new apple silicon chips the  major benefit to this is that apple now  has  full control over the software the chip  and the mac hardware all at the same  time  making it more secure than ever before  in the past  max had a ton of security flaws due to  the intel chips  like meltdown spectre zombie load and  much more and now that apple has finally  ditched intel  they never have to worry about that ever  again and on top of that  the new m1 max now come with built-in  system integrity  and data protection features and apple  is  just getting started so basically the  new transition to apple silicon chips  is the best thing to happen to apple  security in a very long time  which is going to make it even harder  for malware to succeed and  that's why i think the malware numbers  dropped so fast  going into 2021. so with that said if  you currently own  an m1 mac or you're planning on buying  one soon  or maybe one of the future m1x models  don't worry about this whole malware  